    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d358">

                <pb facs="0644" n="512" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv01/pg512"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/6–2545: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 358<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Representative on the Allied
                        Commission on Reparations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pauley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d358-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-25T20:00:00+03:00">June 25, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2262. TopSec from Pauley for Secretary.</p>
                <p>Supplementing my wire of June 19<anchor n="2" xml:id="d358-f2"/> relating to
                    allocation formula foi reparations between the Big Three, after conferring with
                    rep of the <pb facs="0645" n="513" xml:id="pg513"/> UK,<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d358-f3"/> I would now propose that in addition to public statement
                    that Big Three will give up proportionately to other nations as may appear
                    justified, it shall also be understood between the Big Three that unless all of
                    the Big Three ultimately agree on the actual amounts to be allowed other nations
                    and do in fact make such amounts available on the basis of 55, 22½, and 22½
                    percent respectively, then the whole question of distribution of reparations
                    between the Big Three themselves shall be reopened.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d358-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d358-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the Acting Secretary of State over the signature of Harriman.</p>
            </note>
